Subject: [PATCH] Cover the remaining Worker entries and test both V8 fatal
 callbacks

Also carries the test build's api-check event (fork commit 33fee21), which no exported patch held: the series did not reproduce the fork branch without it.

Startup, logging and dynamic import entries that have neither an enclosing scope nor a live originating call now carry the Worker's load identity instead of none: the isolate runs only that Worker's code, and the node still requires a dispatch of the named invocation in the process generation. The test executable can raise V8's API check while a Worker loads, after its top level ran, where only the load's own scope names it.

The process-wide registration goes through one role helper that the constructor calls with V8's registrar. A child-process test reaches the isolate's registered callback through V8's own API check (exit 75, the record, V8's location and message); another captures the callback the ordinary role registers with a mock registrar and calls it as V8 would, and checks that a durable role registers none. The record test also covers a nested scope and another isolate entered on the thread. A unit test checks the identity an entry outside any scope or live call takes, and that a durable role gets none.

